  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A closed 2D Contour now takes a user-set start point with Control or Wear compensation. Before, `pick_ring` refused the pick for both modes.\n- The ring starts at the projection of the pick, as it does with computer compensation.\n- A new module, `contour_comp_pick.rs`, proves the compensation seam law at the pick. `push_span` calls it only for a picked ring. The law has three parts:\n  - The first cut after the G41/G42 engage and the last cut before the G40 cancel are straight moves.\n  - The two cuts are on one line through the seam. Thus the engage offset and the cancel offset are the same.\n  - Under Control only, the programmed part contour is also straight at the seam. Its nearest point is not a part vertex, and its edge is parallel to the first cut.\n- A pick that does not obey the law is refused by name. The refusal is `start point (x, y): <mode> compensation needs the seam on a straight run - ...`. The seam does not move to the automatic mid-run seam.\n- `SpanCtx` has a new field, `picked`. `contour_comp::closest` is now `pub(super)`.\n\n## Cause\n\nItem 4 of #1473 was not done. The automatic compensated seam is put mid-run by `seam_mid_run`, so it obeys the law by construction. A pick can be on a corner arc or on a vertex. The old `push_span` square check can accept a seam on a chord of an outside corner arc, where the nearest part point is the part vertex. Wear had no seam check at all. So a pick needs its own proof before it is taken.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins in `crates/motion/tests/contour_start_comp.rs`. All 5 were red on unchanged code (\"a picked start is not taken with control compensation yet\"):\n- `a_picked_start_under_control_compensation_engages_every_level_at_its_projection`\n- `a_picked_start_under_wear_compensation_engages_every_level_at_its_projection`\n- `a_compensated_pick_on_a_corner_arc_is_refused_by_name_not_moved`\n- `a_compensated_pick_on_a_sharp_corner_is_refused_by_name_not_moved`\n- `a_compensated_pick_mid_run_in_a_bore_is_taken`\n\nNew unit tests in `contour_comp_pick.rs`:\n- `a_straight_centre_chord_over_a_part_vertex_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_seam_mid_run_on_a_straight_wall_holds`\n\nExpected change: `control_compensation_with_a_pick_is_refused_by_name` in `crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs` pinned the old refusal of a mid-run pick. That pick is now taken. The test is renamed `control_compensation_with_a_corner_pick_is_refused_by_name` and picks a corner. The `#[test]` count does not go down.\n\nMutation checks (each guard disabled, then restored):\n- The whole `picked_seam` call removed: the corner-arc, sharp-corner and renamed `contour_start` pins go red. With Wear only, the generator posted a corner seam with 2 spans (\"expected a refusal, got 22 moves with 2 spans\").\n- The collinear-cuts guard removed: `a_compensated_pick_on_a_sharp_corner_is_refused_by_name_not_moved` goes red.\n- The part-vertex guard removed: `a_straight_centre_chord_over_a_part_vertex_is_refused_by_name` goes red. In the generated paths the arc guard fires first, so this guard is a backstop. The unit test pins it directly.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (145 steps, 0 failed, 26.8 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Final-head validation\n\nThe latest review requested the missing heavy validation. No source change was required.\nThe head remains `bc1c6428b7071d740fd19725df24c4d9106a261f`.\nBoth gates selected their plans against `upstream/main` at `a47c7ff222bfdb3d02e25718ba448f5ffe835136`.\nThe shared reference advanced during the quick run. The tested head and working tree stayed unchanged.\nAll checks ran locally in `.claude/worktrees/fix-3350`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: green, exit 0, 241 steps, 0 unexpected failures, 67.2 minutes.\n  - `motion heavy`: 37 steps; 59 tests passed; 2 known tests failed as expected; 0 ignored.\n  - `app heavy`: 203 steps; 46 tests passed; 2 known tests failed as expected; 0 ignored.\n  - The combined release build was the remaining step. Total: 105 tests passed and 4 expected failures.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, exit 0, 145 steps, 0 failures, 26.1 minutes.\n  The 143 suite steps passed 1719 tests and ignored 66 tests. Ignored tests are not passes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green, exit 0, 50.99 seconds.\n\nThe heavy gate isolated these known failures and confirmed their expected red results:\n\n| Issue | Lane | Test | Observed result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #1950 | motion | `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock` | Refused: `hops 10 over 8`. |\n| #1950 | motion | `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note` | Selected `OffsetRings` instead of `Adaptive`. |\n| #1950 | app | `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` | Refused adaptive levels that exceeded the optimal load. |\n| #2849 | app | `fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works` | Failed the selected-face distance assertion: `dist 31.406, r 4`. |\n\nThe six `shared_face_bodies_finish` gouge-check bands passed in 1702.60 seconds.\nThe tracked tree stayed clean. No new pin or mutation was needed for this validation-only finding.\nThe source pins and mutation results above still apply to the unchanged head.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Before this change, no path took a pick under compensation.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The post output of a picked compensated span. The span is the same `CompSpan` type that the automatic seam makes, so the post code path does not change.\n- A picked exit point under compensation. It stays refused by name (the cancel block must leave from the seam of the ring).\n- Items 5 to 7 of #1473 (open chains, tilted contours, other operations). They stay open.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `contour_comp.rs`, `contour_start.rs`, `contour.rs` or `crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs`.\n\nChangelog: A closed 2D Contour takes a picked start point with control or wear compensation; a pick where G41/G42 cannot engage and cancel on one straight run is refused by name.\n\nRefs #1473 (item 4 only; items 5 to 7 stay open, so this PR does not close the issue)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
